{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve been having bad abdominal pain, headaches, and just overall body pain. I feel really weak and nauseous too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The abdominal pain—where exactly is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s in my lower belly, both sides. Not sharp, but constant. And my headaches feel like my usual migraines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fever, chest pain, or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or chest pain. Just some chills now and then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And how has your eating been?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not good. I’ve only been eating toast. Nauseous a lot, and I’ve been vomiting. Also had green diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And when was your last bowel movement?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can’t remember exactly, but it’s been days. Maybe over a week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2182-05-27 14:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks. We’ll check your labs and do an ultrasound to look at your liver and gallbladder since your lipase and alkaline phosphatase were elevated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2182-05-27 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that tell us what’s wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2182-05-27 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps rule out things like gallstones or pancreatitis. But given your history of gastroparesis and constipation, we’re also concerned about bowel issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2182-05-27 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was just here two weeks ago for similar problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2182-05-27 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw that. You had hyponatremia then, which improved with dialysis. Your sodium is better now, but we still need to manage your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your ultrasound came back normal—no gallstones or liver issues. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s mostly due to constipation and your gastroparesis. Your abdomen is soft, no signs of infection. We’ll start a stronger bowel regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what I use at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, plus we’ll add Miralax and lactulose. If that doesn’t work, we may use a soap suds enema, like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2182-05-27 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I remember that helped before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2182-05-27 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed you haven’t had dialysis since before admission. We’d like to do a session tomorrow to help with your overall feeling of malaise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2182-05-27 20:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. I feel so sluggish."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2182-05-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2182-05-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still bloated. Haven’t had a bowel movement yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2182-05-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a soap suds enema this morning. It should help. Also, your labs show your kidney function is stable, and your glucose is manageable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2182-05-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2182-05-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Scheduled for noon today. It should help with your nausea and fatigue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just had a bowel movement! That enema worked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great! That should help your abdominal pain. How’s your headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I took my sumatriptan yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And your leg pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but same as usual. Shooting pains, but no new weakness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2182-05-28 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds like your fibromyalgia. We’ll keep you on your regular meds for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How did the dialysis go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tiring, but I feel a bit clearer now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your labs are improving. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if you keep feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been thinking… I don’t want to be resuscitated if my heart stops. I’ve had enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. We can complete a MOLST form to document that. You’d still want hospitalization if needed, but no CPR or intubation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. I just don’t want extreme measures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2182-05-28 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. I’ll go over the form with you now so you can sign it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Your vitals are stable, and your pain is much improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll send you home with instructions to continue the bowel regimen—Miralax daily, plus your usual meds. And keep up with your peritoneal dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I still use enemas if I get backed up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, as needed. And please follow up with your GI doctor soon. This is the second time in a month, so we need to adjust your plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my headaches and body pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue your sumatriptan for migraines and your regular fibromyalgia meds. If anything worsens, call your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2182-05-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon, including the MOLST form. Take care, and follow up as planned."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2182-05-27 14:36:00",
    "admission_end": "2182-05-29 16:24:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for abdominal pain, headaches, and generalized body pain. Evaluation revealed no acute abdominal pathology on ultrasound, and labs showed stable renal function with mild metabolic acidosis. Abdominal pain was attributed to constipation and gastroparesis, supported by lack of bowel movement for over a week and a reassuring physical exam. She was treated with an intensified bowel regimen including Miralax, lactulose, and a soap suds enema, which resulted in a bowel movement. Peritoneal dialysis was performed to address accumulated uremic symptoms. Her migraines and fibromyalgia pain were managed with home medications and improved during the stay. A MOLST form was completed at her request for DNR/DNI status. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up planned with her PCP and gastroenterologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic autonomic (poly)neuropathy",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Fibromyalgia",
      "Migraine, unspecified, not intractable, without status migrainosus",
      "Dependence on renal dialysis",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis"
    ]
  }
}
